<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Hall of Masks · Sanni Yakuma</title>
<meta name="description" content="Code exorcisms of well-known repositories, after the Sanni Yakuma healing ritual of southern Sri Lanka.">
<style>
{% include "_base.css" %}
header.stage { text-align: center; padding: clamp(48px, 12vh, 140px) 22px clamp(24px, 5vh, 60px); }
header.stage h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 4.4rem); margin: .3em 0 .2em; }
header.stage .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--dim); max-width: 38em; margin: 0 auto; }
.masks-row { display: flex; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; margin: 2em auto 0; max-width: 840px; }
.masks-row svg { width: 38px; height: auto; opacity: .9; }
.hall { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 22px; margin: 6vh 0; }
.card { background: var(--wood); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
.card:hover { border-color: var(--ember); }
.card h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 0 0 .2em; word-break: break-word; }
.card h2 a { color: var(--cream); text-decoration: none; }
.card h2 a::after { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0; }
.card { position: relative; }
.card .count { color: var(--gold); margin: 0 0 .7em; }
.card .demons { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px; margin-bottom: .8em; }
.card .demons svg { width: 40px; height: auto; }
.card .root { font-size: .92rem; color: var(--dim); margin: 0; flex: 1; }
.card .meta { font-size: .8rem; color: var(--dim); margin: .9em 0 0; }
footer { color: var(--dim); font-size: .92rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 40px 22px 70px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header class="stage">
  <p class="kicker">Sanni Yakuma</p>
  <h1>The Hall of Masks</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    In the healing ritual of southern Sri Lanka, eighteen Sanni demons are called out, mocked and sent away.
    Here the patients are well-known open-source repositories. Choose one to watch its exorcism.
  </p>
  <div class="masks-row" aria-hidden="true">{% for m in all_masks %}{{ m }}{% endfor %}</div>
</header>
<main>
  <ul class="hall">
    {% for c in cards %}
    <li class="card">
      <h2><a href="{{ c.href }}">{{ c.r.repo }}</a></h2>
      <p class="count">{{ c.r.possessions | length }} of 18 demons</p>
      <div class="demons">{% for m in c.masks %}{{ m }}{% endfor %}</div>
      <p class="root">{{ c.r.kola_sanniya.root_cause }}</p>
      <p class="meta">{{ c.date }} · {{ c.r.model }}</p>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</main>
<footer>
  <p>
    Every demon in these rituals rests on evidence that plain detectors found in the code; an open Gemma model wrote
    the monologues and the cures, and anything it claimed beyond the evidence was thrown out. The masks are original
    drawings made in code, not copies of real masks.
  </p>
  <p>Perform your own: <a href="https://github.com/dhananjaya-hbc/sanni-yakuma">github.com/dhananjaya-hbc/sanni-yakuma</a></p>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
